;; bedit-agent — coding agents in bedit, as a hive PLUGIN package (`:enhances bedit`). A
;; session is an agent working in one project under a PROFILE the project defines
;; (.bedit-agent.blsp), several at once per project. Two front ends over the same profiles
;; and the same tools: `:chat`, a bedit buffer where every tool the agent has is bedit's (it
;; sees your unsaved buffers, edits through them, asks you in the echo area), and `:tui`, the
;; agent's own terminal interface in a terminal buffer with bedit's tools added. The first
;; backend is Claude Code on the SUBSCRIPTION (agentkit); the tools, profiles and sessions
;; are the agent-neutral part.
(project
  :name "bedit-agent"
  :version "0.1.0"
  :brood ">= 0.50.0"
  :description
    "Coding agents in bedit: per-project profiles, several sessions per project, a chat buffer where every tool is bedit's, or the agent's own terminal UI with bedit's tools added. Claude Code on the subscription first."
  :repository "https://github.com/broodlang/bedit-agent"
  :enhances {bedit ">= 0.9"}
  :dependencies [[agentkit :version "0.1.0"]]
  :dev-dependencies [[bedit :path "../bedit"]]
  :source-paths ["src"])
